{"id": "police-captains-overtime-in-lieu", "title": "Police Captains trade overtime for 8% more pay, then earn $779,710 of it", "seconds": 113.0, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "16bf4012020b280b", "words": 345, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "What did police Captains get in 2007 for giving up overtime?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.71, "shot": "c0", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["8%", "more"], "sub": "in lieu of overtime, since 2007"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.63, 1.04, 1.25, 1.34, 1.5, 1.85, 2.16, 2.29, 2.52, 2.66]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "An 8 percent raise, in lieu of overtime.", "t0": 3.71, "t1": 5.69, "shot": "c0", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["8%", "more"], "sub": "in lieu of overtime, since 2007"}, "emph": ["8 percent"], "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.35, 0.68, 1.08, 1.24, 1.4, 1.5]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "oneLine"], "text": "Yet in fiscal 2026,", "t0": 6.11, "t1": 7.87, "shot": "c1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$779,710", "label": "overtime on Captain 3 rows, fiscal 2026", "sub": "a rank paid 8% more in lieu of overtime"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.38, 0.79, 1.07]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "oneLine"], "text": "Captain 3 rows carried 779,710 dollars of overtime.", "t0": 7.87, "t1": 13.21, "shot": "c1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$779,710", "label": "overtime on Captain 3 rows, fiscal 2026", "sub": "a rank paid 8% more in lieu of overtime"}, "emph": ["779,710"], "wt": [0.04, 0.43, 0.73, 1.1, 1.43, 1.74, 2.05, 2.66, 3.51, 3.85, 4.13, 4.36, 4.68, 4.79]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 13.63, "t1": 15.25, "shot": "c2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.29, 0.37, 0.94, 1.11, 1.18]}, {"scene": "trade", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "timeline[0]"], "text": "Human Resources priced the overtime Captains gave up at about 12 percent of pay.", "t0": 15.47, "t1": 19.32, "shot": "c3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "n07", "kicker": "Human Resources, Overview Presentation on Bargaining 2007", "text": "Captains will be given an 8% wage adjustment to offset the loss of paid overtime, valued at around 12%, resulting in approximately $150,000 in annual savings.", "mark": "valued at around 12%"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.81, 1.12, 1.24, 1.72, 2.19, 2.4, 2.55, 2.64, 2.85, 3.12, 3.42, 3.54]}, {"scene": "trade", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The trade was to save the City about 150,000 dollars a year.", "t0": 19.44, "t1": 23.01, "shot": "c3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "n07", "kicker": "Human Resources, Overview Presentation on Bargaining 2007", "text": "Captains will be given an 8% wage adjustment to offset the loss of paid overtime, valued at around 12%, resulting in approximately $150,000 in annual savings.", "mark": "valued at around 12%"}, "emph": ["150,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.57, 0.7, 0.94, 1.06, 1.38, 1.67, 1.88, 2.17, 2.49, 2.82, 3.14, 3.22]}, {"scene": "trade", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[6]", "links[0]"], "text": "Every police agreement since has kept the clause, including the one for 2026 to 2030.", "t0": 23.13, "t1": 28.18, "shot": "c4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Captains will receive an eight percent (8%) wage increase in lieu of earning overtime or compensatory time off", "kicker": "Police agreement 2026-2030, paragraphs 199-200"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.66, 1.09, 1.4, 1.54, 1.74, 1.84, 2.53, 2.97, 3.1, 3.27, 3.41, 3.69, 4.29, 4.4, 4.65]}, {"scene": "trade", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "innocent[0]"], "text": "One door stays open: 10B, off-duty work that outside hirers pay the City for.", "t0": 28.3, "t1": 32.96, "shot": "c5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "10B work", "sub": "off-duty jobs that outside hirers pay the City for"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.43, 0.7, 1.3, 2.23, 2.71, 2.91, 3.08, 3.46, 3.86, 4.02, 4.12, 4.36]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["suspicious[1].title", "timeline[1]"], "text": "In fiscal 2013 to 2016, Captain 3 overtime was about 17,000 dollars a year.", "t0": 33.18, "t1": 38.86, "shot": "c6", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["About", "$17,000"], "sub": "a year, fiscal 2013 to 2016"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.65, 0.98, 1.39, 1.47, 1.73, 2.6, 3.0, 3.3, 3.84, 3.97, 4.23, 4.66, 4.98, 5.27, 5.36]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Then it climbed.", "t0": 38.98, "t1": 40.68, "shot": "c7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Overtime on Captain 3 rows", "rows": [["FY2019", "$59,098"], ["FY2023", "$299,857"], ["FY2024", "$459,456"], ["FY2025", "$154,662"], ["FY2026", "$779,710"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.22]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "By fiscal 2024 it had reached 459,456 dollars.", "t0": 40.68, "t1": 46.25, "shot": "c7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Overtime on Captain 3 rows", "rows": [["FY2019", "$59,098"], ["FY2023", "$299,857"], ["FY2024", "$459,456"], ["FY2025", "$154,662"], ["FY2026", "$779,710"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.59, 0.85, 1.53, 1.65, 1.77, 2.06, 2.34, 2.64, 3.22, 4.05, 4.28, 4.51, 5.03]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "After a dip in 2025, fiscal 2026 reached 779,710.", "t0": 46.37, "t1": 53.18, "shot": "c7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Overtime on Captain 3 rows", "rows": [["FY2019", "$59,098"], ["FY2023", "$299,857"], ["FY2024", "$459,456"], ["FY2025", "$154,662"], ["FY2026", "$779,710"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.34, 0.59, 0.68, 0.99, 1.9, 2.36, 2.66, 3.49, 3.8, 4.16, 4.57, 5.15, 5.6, 5.86, 6.08]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "How far above the old level?", "t0": 53.18, "t1": 54.9, "shot": "c7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Overtime on Captain 3 rows", "rows": [["FY2019", "$59,098"], ["FY2023", "$299,857"], ["FY2024", "$459,456"], ["FY2025", "$154,662"], ["FY2026", "$779,710"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.44, 0.67, 0.78, 0.96]}, {"scene": "climb", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "36 to 51 times higher.", "t0": 54.9, "t1": 56.71, "shot": "c8", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "36 to 51×", "label": "fiscal 2026 against fiscal 2013-2016", "sub": "Captain 3 overtime"}, "emph": ["51 times"], "wt": [0.04, 0.63, 0.75, 1.2, 1.47]}, {"scene": "rows", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "It was not one Captain: 29 of the 36 Captain 3 rows had some overtime.", "t0": 57.23, "t1": 62.62, "shot": "c9", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "29 of 36", "label": "Captain 3 rows with overtime, fiscal 2026", "sub": "Controller’s payroll, job Q082"}, "emph": ["29 of the 36"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.3, 0.59, 0.77, 1.76, 2.51, 2.63, 2.76, 3.33, 3.73, 4.01, 4.43, 4.63, 4.82]}, {"scene": "rows", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "The largest row had more overtime than salary: 259,425 dollars.", "t0": 62.74, "t1": 69.32, "shot": "c10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Overtime, largest Captain 3 row", "$259,425"], "b": ["Salary, same row", "$247,817"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2026 · 3,975 paid hours"}, "emph": ["259,425"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.54, 0.83, 0.99, 1.19, 1.66, 1.83, 2.77, 3.07, 3.39, 3.99, 4.74, 5.01, 5.29, 5.93]}, {"scene": "rows", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "That row was paid for 3,975 hours in the year.", "t0": 69.44, "t1": 73.25, "shot": "c10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Overtime, largest Captain 3 row", "$259,425"], "b": ["Salary, same row", "$247,817"], "kicker": "Fiscal 2026 · 3,975 paid hours"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.45, 0.59, 0.8, 0.96, 1.24, 1.73, 2.03, 2.39, 2.98, 3.31, 3.4, 3.51]}, {"scene": "commanders", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "story[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "One rank up, Commanders work under an agreement with no overtime clause at all.", "t0": 73.47, "t1": 77.04, "shot": "c11", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Commander 3 rows (job 0490)", "sub": "Managers’ agreement: no overtime clause", "rows": [["Overtime, fiscal 2026", "$91,007"], ["Rows with overtime", "7 of 14"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.47, 0.72, 1.18, 1.47, 1.69, 1.77, 2.16, 2.34, 2.52, 2.95, 3.23, 3.33]}, {"scene": "commanders", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "links[2]"], "text": "Their rows still carried 91,007 dollars of overtime in fiscal 2026.", "t0": 77.16, "t1": 81.79, "shot": "c11", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Commander 3 rows (job 0490)", "sub": "Managers’ agreement: no overtime clause", "rows": [["Overtime, fiscal 2026", "$91,007"], ["Rows with overtime", "7 of 14"]]}, "emph": ["91,007"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.47, 0.72, 1.05, 1.57, 2.0, 2.26, 2.56, 2.67, 3.15, 3.28, 3.71, 3.99]}, {"scene": "tenb", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "story[3]", "timeline[2]"], "text": "The plain explanation is 10B, which grew with the retail-theft patrols after 2021.", "t0": 82.01, "t1": 86.84, "shot": "c12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Retail-theft patrols", "sub": "funded in large part through 10B, since 2021"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.4, 0.97, 1.12, 1.9, 2.15, 2.37, 2.54, 2.66, 3.22, 3.72, 3.98, 4.27]}, {"scene": "tenb", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[3]", "timeline[4]", "links[3]"], "text": "The Department counted about 88,000 hours of 10B in fiscal 2024-25.", "t0": 86.96, "t1": 92.01, "shot": "c13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "88,000", "label": "hours of 10B, fiscal 2024-25", "sub": "Police Department staffing analysis, 2025"}, "emph": ["88,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.52, 0.81, 1.04, 1.46, 1.82, 2.17, 2.28, 2.73, 2.87, 3.36, 3.71, 4.35, 4.45]}, {"scene": "tenb", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[3]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "But the payroll has no code that separates 10B from other overtime.", "t0": 92.13, "t1": 95.59, "shot": "c14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "No 10B code", "sub": "the payroll does not separate 10B from other overtime"}, "emph": ["no code"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.19, 0.55, 0.75, 0.96, 1.25, 1.4, 1.85, 2.44, 2.67, 2.92]}, {"scene": "tenb", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["story[4]", "timeline[3]"], "text": "And the 2024 audit found the Department’s overtime limits were not enforced.", "t0": 95.71, "t1": 99.72, "shot": "c15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "aud", "kicker": "Performance Audit of Police Department Overtime, 2024-12-12", "text": "captains receive a wage increase in lieu of earning paid overtime or compensatory time off", "mark": "in lieu of earning paid overtime"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.22, 0.51, 0.97, 1.27, 1.47, 1.57, 2.06, 2.49, 2.98, 3.19, 3.35]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The records don’t show how much of it is 10B, or who approved it.", "t0": 99.94, "t1": 102.91, "shot": "c16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["How much of the overtime is 10B work", "Who approved it, and under which rule", "Whether any is late pay for an earlier rank"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.62, 0.79, 0.9, 1.07, 1.15, 1.25, 1.36, 2.16, 2.33, 2.48, 2.86]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The 10B assignment records, and overtime by code and approver.", "t0": 103.03, "t1": 106.98, "shot": "c17", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "10B assignment records for Captains and Commanders"}, {"who": "", "what": "Overtime by earnings code and by approver"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.27, 0.55, 1.1, 1.27, 1.59, 1.98, 2.36, 2.49, 2.93, 3.09, 3.33, 3.43]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "No authority has made a finding, and no officer is accused here.", "t0": 107.1, "t1": 110.0, "shot": "c18", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.54, 0.65, 0.8, 0.87, 1.48, 1.7, 1.87, 2.25, 2.34, 2.67]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 110.12, "t1": 112.08, "shot": "c19", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.45, 0.52, 1.06, 1.26, 1.35]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "8% more", "trade": "The trade · 2007", "climb": "The climb", "rows": "Most Captains", "commanders": "One rank up", "tenb": "The 10B question", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "question"}